This product is a Cangjie (仓颉) port of the EU Digital Identity Wallet
OpenID4VCI and OpenID4VP / SIOPv2 libraries for Swift:

    eudi-lib-ios-openid4vci-swift
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-ios-openid4vci-swift

    eudi-lib-ios-siop-openid4vp-swift
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-ios-siop-openid4vp-swift

The protocol logic (credential offer resolution, authorization, PKCE, DPoP,
credential requests, presentation request resolution and response) is
reimplemented in Cangjie with the original Swift sources used as the
reference implementation.

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software:

  - eudi_lib_core_crypto (Apache License 2.0; consumed as a sibling
    third_party checkout, not vendored) — ECDSA P-256 / ECDH / AES-GCM /
    digest / JWS primitives backed by Cangjie stdx.crypto.

  - eudi_lib_jose, eudi_lib_sdjwt, eudi_lib_x509 (Apache License 2.0;
    consumed as sibling third_party checkouts, not vendored).

  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache License 2.0) — Cangjie extended standard
    library runtime, bundled under entry/libs/stdx/. See the LICENSE file
    shipped inside the upstream cangjie-stdx release archive.

  - OpenSSL runtime libraries (libcrypto_openssl.z.so, libssl_openssl.z.so,
    Apache License 2.0) and libsecurec.so, bundled under
    entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device execution of stdx.crypto.

